    <p>I don't know if they are animals called seals or not precisely, but let's assume they are seals. The same-looking animals are symbols or official character of South Seattle College (It might be Seattle South College. I'm not sure.) But they must be sea otters. Does anybody know what are the differences?</p>
    <p>Next time seeing any animals other than monekeys and humans, I want to try imagining what if my legs and arms are like theirs (But when I am really bored and have plenty of time, though.) Then looking again these seals, what a tragedy if my arms and legs become those of them! I cannot wash my body well nor I cannot stand up straightforward. How do they live with them? Does anybody know?</p>
